  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Hello. \nEver since i got my new PC VRChat has issues with certain worlds. If i enter a world sometimes VRChat starts to heat up my PC without a reason to sometimes above 80% GPU Usage constantly until i leave the world, then it's going quite as my PC would be just idling. Rejoining the exact same world again sometimes fixes this but not always. This happens in Desktop being alone entering my homeworld already. I been in world's with tons of people in VR having no issues at all but some world's turn my PC into a starting airplane and i can't figure out the reason as this is randomly happening only on some worlds. This been the case for a half year atleast. \nMy Specs:\n-Intel Core i9-11900F\n-MSI Z590 PLUS, S. 1200\n-Nvidia Geforce RTX 3070 Ti 8GB\n-32GB Corsair Vengeance DDR4\n-2TB Samsung SSD, M.2\nI tried resetting VRChat and Reinstalled Windows 11 but that didn't change anything. \nIf anyone knows a fix or the reason this could happen please let me know!",
